{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"397","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. On Segment's Own Points"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Our old friend Alexey has finally entered the University of City N — the Berland capital. Alexey expected his father to get him a place to live in but his father said it was high time for Alexey to practice some financial independence. So, Alexey is living in a dorm. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The dorm has exactly one straight dryer — a "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":" centimeter long rope to hang clothes on. The dryer has got a coordinate system installed: the leftmost end of the dryer has coordinate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":", and the opposite end has coordinate "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"100"},{"kind":"text","text":". Overall, the university has "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" students. Dean's office allows "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th student to use the segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(li, ri)"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the dryer. However, the dean's office actions are contradictory and now one part of the dryer can belong to multiple students!"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alexey don't like when someone touch his clothes. That's why he want make it impossible to someone clothes touch his ones. So Alexey wonders: what is the total length of the parts of the dryer that he may use in a such way that clothes of the others "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(n - 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" students aren't drying there. Help him! Note that Alexey, as the most respected student, has number 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a positive integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i + 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th line contains integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"li"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ri"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ li < ri ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the endpoints of the corresponding segment for the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th student."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On a single line print a single number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":", equal to the sum of lengths of the parts of the dryer which are inside Alexey's segment and are outside all other segments."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n0 5\n2 8\n1 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n0 10\n1 5\n7 15\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that it's not important are clothes drying on the touching segments (e.g. "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 2)"},{"kind":"text","text":") considered to be touching or not because you need to find the length of segments."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test sample Alexey may use the only segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":". In such case his clothes will not touch clothes on the segments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1, 6)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2, 8)"},{"kind":"text","text":". The length of segment "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" is 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test sample Alexey may dry his clothes on segments "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(0, 1)"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(5, 7)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Overall length of these segments is 3."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"397A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/397/problem/A"}